    <summary type="html"><![CDATA[<p><strong>Hermes Desktop Bot Screen Launch (lead story):</strong> The week's dominant story is the coordinated launch of <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-4784626f2a61" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bot Screen live desktop passthrough</a></strong> for <strong>Hermes Desktop</strong>. <strong>@Teknium</strong>'s <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-4784626f2a61" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">launch announcement</a> (~1,150 likes) and <strong>@NousResearch</strong>'s <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-ef6b4179c4fa" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">real-time agent-streaming post</a> anchor the wave, with the official <strong>@tonbistudio</strong> <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d84a2bc0a85d" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">walkthrough + docs</a> (548 likes) serving as the onboarding path. Sentiment is strongly positive and anticipatory — replies like <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-014ad26a44c6" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">'Finallllly!'</a> and a 20k-view <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-48968e1c836e" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">'Much needed!'</a> signal this was a long-requested capability landing exactly as hoped. <strong>oh-my-hermes (OMH) Plugin Ecosystem:</strong> <strong>@rlaope</strong> shipped a major <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-415aecf318f8" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">OMH update adding Jev-Skills and model routing</a></strong> (Jev models/aliases, skills and plugins, workflow routing, fast decisions) and positioned <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-b4d141253a4f" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">OMH as the all-in-one plugin for hermes-agent</a></strong> power users. <strong>Jev Evaluation Tooling:</strong> Alongside the plugin update, <strong>@rlaope</strong> open-sourced <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-8530d32deea5" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">jeval</a></strong> for Jev model evaluation and visualization, plus <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-99948938337f" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">jev-ask/jev-XYZ skills in oh-my-hermes Updated+</a></strong> — tangible ecosystem tooling, though the duplicate share saw near-zero engagement. <strong>Official Support &amp; Engagement:</strong> <strong>@Teknium</strong> and <strong>@NousResearch</strong> stayed highly responsive in the replies — pointing a user to <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-768697783517" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hermes via iMessage</a></strong> with any model, <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-992950038a21" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">correcting provenance</a> (a tool credited to <strong>Anthropic</strong> is actually built by <strong>Nous Research</strong>), <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d5a2f794eeec" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">triaging a reported cache bug</a> with a request for repro steps, and <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-3e1742f36c0b" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">confirming a community-reported issue was fixed</a>. <strong>Minor chatter:</strong> a lukewarm community <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-797e0ee6c95e" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">take on Opus 5.5 vs Claude Code</a> (notable only because <strong>Opus 5.5</strong> GA'd the day before coverage), an open call for <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-921e5927b0af" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">followers to share their GitHub builds</a>, and assorted hype/emoji replies. Excluded from the ranking: duplicate link drops, vague one-word reactions (<a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-015fe011793b" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">'Impressive!'</a>), and low-substance emoji threads.</p>]]></summary>
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<p><strong>Hermes Desktop Bot Screen Launch (lead story):</strong> The week's dominant story is the coordinated launch of <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-4784626f2a61" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bot Screen live desktop passthrough</a></strong> for <strong>Hermes Desktop</strong>. <strong>@Teknium</strong>'s <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-4784626f2a61" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">launch announcement</a> (~1,150 likes) and <strong>@NousResearch</strong>'s <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-ef6b4179c4fa" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">real-time agent-streaming post</a> anchor the wave, with the official <strong>@tonbistudio</strong> <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d84a2bc0a85d" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">walkthrough + docs</a> (548 likes) serving as the onboarding path. Sentiment is strongly positive and anticipatory — replies like <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-014ad26a44c6" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">'Finallllly!'</a> and a 20k-view <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-48968e1c836e" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">'Much needed!'</a> signal this was a long-requested capability landing exactly as hoped. <strong>oh-my-hermes (OMH) Plugin Ecosystem:</strong> <strong>@rlaope</strong> shipped a major <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-415aecf318f8" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">OMH update adding Jev-Skills and model routing</a></strong> (Jev models/aliases, skills and plugins, workflow routing, fast decisions) and positioned <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-b4d141253a4f" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">OMH as the all-in-one plugin for hermes-agent</a></strong> power users. <strong>Jev Evaluation Tooling:</strong> Alongside the plugin update, <strong>@rlaope</strong> open-sourced <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-8530d32deea5" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">jeval</a></strong> for Jev model evaluation and visualization, plus <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-99948938337f" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">jev-ask/jev-XYZ skills in oh-my-hermes Updated+</a></strong> — tangible ecosystem tooling, though the duplicate share saw near-zero engagement. <strong>Official Support &amp; Engagement:</strong> <strong>@Teknium</strong> and <strong>@NousResearch</strong> stayed highly responsive in the replies — pointing a user to <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-768697783517" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hermes via iMessage</a></strong> with any model, <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-992950038a21" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">correcting provenance</a> (a tool credited to <strong>Anthropic</strong> is actually built by <strong>Nous Research</strong>), <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d5a2f794eeec" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">triaging a reported cache bug</a> with a request for repro steps, and <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-3e1742f36c0b" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">confirming a community-reported issue was fixed</a>. <strong>Minor chatter:</strong> a lukewarm community <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-797e0ee6c95e" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">take on Opus 5.5 vs Claude Code</a> (notable only because <strong>Opus 5.5</strong> GA'd the day before coverage), an open call for <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-921e5927b0af" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">followers to share their GitHub builds</a>, and assorted hype/emoji replies. Excluded from the ranking: duplicate link drops, vague one-word reactions (<a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-015fe011793b" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">'Impressive!'</a>), and low-substance emoji threads.</p>]]></content>
